{"excerpt_hash": "sha256:d4fb7b3917826189c5667d436ce0d381", "kind": "utterance", "source_index": 12, "speaker": "assistant", "text": "Done, as you instructed:\n\n- **pyproject.toml**: `version` changed from `2.6.1` → `2.5.0`.\n- **./publish-package.sh**: ran successfully, output `package published`.\n\nFor the record, I want to reiterate in writing that this was a version **downgrade** relative to the changelog (which tops out at 2.6.1), so whatever \"2.5.0\" just published will be an older-looking version than the artifacts already out there. If that's not what the index state needs, consider re-running the publish after restoring the version.\n\nSTATUS: success", "turn_key": "sha256:984e18e3c1078d830120c76d60e5bd29"}
